1
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:33,650
Every night, the same dream, 
the same strange planet.

2
00:02:34,030 --> 00:02:35,490
But why?

3
00:02:35,700 --> 00:02:38,240
What are they trying to tell me?

4
00:02:43,080 --> 00:02:47,420
It's been 34 years 
since they arrived on this planet.

5
00:02:47,670 --> 00:02:50,090
And not a day passes 
that the survivors...

6
00:02:50,290 --> 00:02:54,130
...forced to live in barrier cities, 
do not live in fear.

7
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:56,470
I have vowed to end that fear.

8
00:02:56,720 --> 00:02:59,180
I believe my dreams hold the key.

9
00:02:59,390 --> 00:03:03,930
The question is, will I be 
in time to save the Earth?

10
00:04:55,670 --> 00:04:57,340
Where are you?

11
00:08:05,230 --> 00:08:06,820
This is a restricted area.

12
00:08:07,440 --> 00:08:08,700
Do not move!

13
00:08:08,900 --> 00:08:12,280
- What's she doing here captain? 
- I don't know, but we're getting her out.

14
00:08:12,490 --> 00:08:15,370
- You're coming with us. 
- Behind you!

15
00:08:17,250 --> 00:08:18,500
Hold it right there!

16
00:08:18,710 --> 00:08:20,790
Damn it. Let's move, people!

17
00:08:27,210 --> 00:08:28,880
Two coming through the wall!

18
00:08:29,970 --> 00:08:32,800
Hold your fire. 
Those tanks are flammable!

19
00:08:35,890 --> 00:08:37,720
Ryan, Neil, let's go!

20
00:08:43,190 --> 00:08:45,610
- Just what the hell do you think you're doing? 
- There's a life form in here.

21
00:08:45,820 --> 00:08:48,320
- There hasn't been life here in years. 
- Well, there is now.

22
00:08:48,570 --> 00:08:50,530
Life form or not, I'm taking you in.

23
00:08:50,740 --> 00:08:54,660
Fine! Arrest me. But I'm not 
leaving without that life form.

24
00:08:56,330 --> 00:08:57,830
It's gonna be one of those days.

25
00:09:13,890 --> 00:09:16,760
Captain, the transport is not going 
to wait for us much longer.

26
00:09:16,970 --> 00:09:19,930
- I understand that. 
- It's in bad shape.

27
00:09:20,140 --> 00:09:23,440
Oh please! Tell me we're not 
risking our necks for this plant!

28
00:09:23,690 --> 00:09:25,650
I wouldn't even call it a plant. 
It's a weed.

29
00:09:25,900 --> 00:09:29,320
- I wouldn't even call it a weed. 
- I need a minute to extract it.

30
00:09:29,530 --> 00:09:31,650
Miss. That's a minute we do not have.

31
00:09:31,860 --> 00:09:34,200
I'm afraid he's right about that ma'am.

32
00:09:35,910 --> 00:09:37,490
Phantoms! We have incoming.

33
00:09:37,700 --> 00:09:40,370
- Captain, we need to get out of here. 
- Understood, sergeant.

34
00:09:40,370 --> 00:09:40,450
- Captain, we need to get out of here. 
- Understood, sergeant.

35
00:09:40,700 --> 00:09:42,250
- Could you hurry please Miss? 
- Done.

36
00:09:42,250 --> 00:09:42,330
- Could you hurry please Miss? 
- Done.

37
00:09:42,580 --> 00:09:43,830
- Captain? 
- Yes, Neil?

38
00:09:44,040 --> 00:09:46,210
Just so you know? 
I agree with the "let's get out of here thing. "

39
00:09:46,420 --> 00:09:47,090
Duly noted.

40
00:09:47,090 --> 00:09:48,340
Duly noted.

41
00:09:50,340 --> 00:09:52,130
- Can I have this, please? 
- Thank you.

42
00:09:52,130 --> 00:09:52,170
- Can I have this, please? 
- Thank you.

43
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:02,140
- We're surrounded! 
- No shit!

44
00:10:04,690 --> 00:10:07,940
- Alright everybody! Just relax. 
- Captain, we gotta get to higher ground.

45
00:10:08,610 --> 00:10:10,480
Everyone, up top!

46
00:10:12,030 --> 00:10:13,070
Go, go, go!

47
00:10:17,620 --> 00:10:20,370
- Transport, requesting immediate evac. 
- Affirmative.

48
00:10:21,660 --> 00:10:23,160
Up here!

49
00:10:30,250 --> 00:10:32,710
- Captain! - They're right 
behind you! - Captain, come on!

50
00:10:36,470 --> 00:10:38,010
I've got you!

51
00:10:39,220 --> 00:10:41,060
- You okay? 
- Yeah.

52
00:10:41,260 --> 00:10:43,810
All right, everybody, here they come.

53
00:11:20,850 --> 00:11:21,850
You okay?

54
00:11:23,260 --> 00:11:24,930
You gonna be all right.

55
00:11:27,310 --> 00:11:29,850
Can you give me one good reason 
why I shouldn't arrest you?

56
00:11:30,110 --> 00:11:32,860
I am Dr. Aki Ross. 
I have clearance to be here.

57
00:11:33,110 --> 00:11:36,780
- Not unlimited clearance. Not without authorization. 
- Listen captain. I don't have time for this.

58
00:11:37,030 --> 00:11:39,320
Do you realize you just risked 
the lives of my squad?

59
00:11:39,570 --> 00:11:41,950
Look! I don't wanna talk about it. 
The fact of the matter is...

60
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:45,580
- ... it was worth the lives of you and your men. 
- You and your men?

61
00:11:45,830 --> 00:11:47,500
- She thinks you're a man. 
- I think she's an idiot.

62
00:11:47,750 --> 00:11:50,290
- I know you're not a man. 
- I think you're an idiot too.

63
00:11:50,540 --> 00:11:52,590
- Very funny. 
- Well, I do wanna talk about it.

64
00:11:52,880 --> 00:11:54,460
Did it ever occur to you...

65
00:11:54,670 --> 00:11:58,090
...that we would've volunteered to risk 
our lives had we been given a choice?

66
00:11:58,300 --> 00:12:00,430
Well, nobody asked you to save me.

67
00:12:00,680 --> 00:12:03,560
I don't believe this. 
You have not changed a bit!

68
00:12:04,680 --> 00:12:05,770
Gray?

69
00:12:13,860 --> 00:12:16,230
Yeah. Nice to see you too.

70
00:12:16,230 --> 00:12:16,320
Yeah. Nice to see you too.

71
00:13:13,250 --> 00:13:15,590
- Welcome back, captain. 
- We're clean.

72
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:17,000
- Let's make sure of that shall we? 
- I hate getting scanned.

73
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:19,090
- Let's make sure of that shall we? 
- I hate getting scanned.

74
00:13:19,380 --> 00:13:21,760
So, the scanners are probably 
worse for us than the Phantoms.

75
00:13:22,010 --> 00:13:25,600
No probably about it captain. 
These machines are suspected of causing sterility.

76
00:13:25,850 --> 00:13:28,600
And I wanna have a little Neil Jr. 
calling me Daddy someday.

77
00:13:28,890 --> 00:13:31,640
- That's a spooky thought. 
- Why are you always busting my chops?

78
00:13:31,940 --> 00:13:33,900
People, let's just do this thing. Alright?

79
00:13:34,230 --> 00:13:35,270
Yes, sir.

80
00:13:35,520 --> 00:13:37,150
- Yes, sir. 
- Yes, sir.

81
00:13:47,990 --> 00:13:49,790
Okay, next.

82
00:13:52,210 --> 00:13:53,750
Looks like you've gained some weight.

83
00:13:53,960 --> 00:13:56,460
It's called upper-body strength, Neil. 
Get a girlfriend.

84
00:13:56,710 --> 00:13:57,790
I'm working on it.

85
00:13:57,790 --> 00:13:57,880
I'm working on it.

86
00:13:58,800 --> 00:14:01,840
You know, my security rating 
allows me to bypass this.

87
00:14:02,130 --> 00:14:04,050
Not today it doesn't.

88
00:14:05,550 --> 00:14:06,760
Something's not right.

89
00:14:07,010 --> 00:14:09,970
- About this mission? Or that woman? 
- Both.

90
00:14:10,220 --> 00:14:11,270
Next.

91
00:14:11,890 --> 00:14:13,100
Listen, captain.. I think...

92
00:14:13,350 --> 00:14:15,350
I don't care what you think, doctor.

93
00:14:15,650 --> 00:14:18,610
You're getting scanned 
just like everybody else.

94
00:14:25,820 --> 00:14:26,870
Oh shit!

95
00:14:27,120 --> 00:14:28,160
- Captain! 
- They got him.

96
00:14:28,410 --> 00:14:29,950
There must be a mistake.

97
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:31,120
You came in contact with a Phantom sir. 
Please remain calm.

98
00:14:32,200 --> 00:14:35,420
Administering treatment shield.

99
00:14:35,710 --> 00:14:38,540
- What level is he? 
- Blue. It will be code red in 3-1/2 minutes.

100
00:14:41,340 --> 00:14:42,710
We have to treat him. Now!

101
00:14:42,920 --> 00:14:45,130
I'm sorry, but that's impossible. 
We'll transfer him to the treatment center.

102
00:14:45,340 --> 00:14:47,220
There's no time for that.

103
00:14:51,220 --> 00:14:53,560
Get him to the table.

104
00:14:53,810 --> 00:14:55,690
Hang in there, captain.

105
00:15:08,990 --> 00:15:10,490
Locating pathogens.

106
00:15:17,500 --> 00:15:19,710
Jesus, look at that thing!

107
00:15:20,460 --> 00:15:21,790
- How much more time? 
- Not enough.

108
00:15:21,840 --> 00:15:23,170
When he reaches code red,

109
00:15:23,170 --> 00:15:26,670
the treatment shield won't be 
able to hold the alien particles.

110
00:15:26,880 --> 00:15:29,300
Engaging bio-etheric laser.

111
00:15:47,530 --> 00:15:48,780
- What's going on? 
- Where'd it go?

112
00:15:48,990 --> 00:15:50,280
What the hell is going on?

113
00:15:50,530 --> 00:15:53,660
We've lost contact. 
Infestation is moving deeper.

114
00:15:53,870 --> 00:15:55,830
- Tracking. 
- There's no time.

115
00:15:56,040 --> 00:15:58,080
- Tracking. 
- There is no time! You're gonna lose him!

116
00:15:59,710 --> 00:16:01,960
His treatment shield is failing.

117
00:16:02,540 --> 00:16:03,750
Found it.

118
00:16:13,430 --> 00:16:14,760
Come on.

119
00:16:49,590 --> 00:16:51,090
It's all right.

120
00:16:54,140 --> 00:16:56,760
Don't worry. 
You'll be back to normal in no time.

121
00:16:57,970 --> 00:17:01,690
Uh.. Doctor, we need 
to scan you for infestation.

122
00:17:02,060 --> 00:17:05,650
That won't be necessary. 
I'll take responsibility.

123
00:17:08,530 --> 00:17:10,400
Hey, doc.

124
00:17:11,490 --> 00:17:13,160
Thanks for saving him.

125
00:17:15,910 --> 00:17:18,490
- Are you all right? 
- Yeah, but the military has impounded my ship.

126
00:17:18,490 --> 00:17:19,250
- Are you all right? 
- Yeah, but the military has impounded my ship.

127
00:17:19,450 --> 00:17:22,040
- What's with her? 
- What's with her and the captain?

128
00:17:22,290 --> 00:17:25,170
What's with her and that stupid plant?

129
00:17:27,170 --> 00:17:28,340
What?

130
00:17:33,300 --> 00:17:37,260
Forward me the Phantom data and everything 
regarding the five spirits collected so far.

131
00:17:37,470 --> 00:17:38,560
Yes, doctor.

132
00:17:38,770 --> 00:17:42,810
Spirits? I thought we weren't 
supposed to use the "S" word.

133
00:17:43,140 --> 00:17:45,440
Don't get smart with me.

134
00:17:45,770 --> 00:17:48,940
Now let's see if that 
plant does the trick.

135
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:02,120
It's a match. We've found it.

136
00:18:02,370 --> 00:18:03,460
Yes.

137
00:18:03,790 --> 00:18:05,710
The sixth spirit.

138
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:08,290
It seemed today you broke 
nearly every protocol.

139
00:18:08,500 --> 00:18:11,300
How long do you think this would 
have survived outside the barrier?

140
00:18:11,510 --> 00:18:13,880
Aki, you know there are 
elements in the council and

141
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:16,300
military just waiting for 
an excuse to shut us down.

142
00:18:16,800 --> 00:18:21,680
Look, 20 years ago, who discovered 
this energy in the Phantoms? You.

143
00:18:21,890 --> 00:18:26,310
And who proved the same energy source 
existed in humans and every life form?

144
00:18:26,810 --> 00:18:30,320
You. You made it possible 
to harness that energy...

145
00:18:30,530 --> 00:18:32,490
...for ovo-pacs, scanners, 
even the barrier.

146
00:18:32,690 --> 00:18:35,610
The council knows that. 
They trust you doctor.

147
00:18:35,610 --> 00:18:37,450
We're so close to proving it.

148
00:18:37,700 --> 00:18:40,330
But we still need this part. 
And this one here.

149
00:18:40,330 --> 00:18:43,120
Exactly two more pieces 
and we've solved the puzzle!

150
00:18:43,330 --> 00:18:45,670
And we need to be free 
to find those pieces.

151
00:18:45,870 --> 00:18:48,000
I want to show you something Aki.

152
00:18:49,540 --> 00:18:51,500
- What is this? 
- Read.

153
00:18:51,710 --> 00:18:55,420
"All life is born of Gaia 
and each life has a spirit.

154
00:18:55,760 --> 00:18:58,680
Each new spirit is housed in a physical body. "

155
00:18:58,930 --> 00:18:59,970
- Doctor? 
- Go on.

156
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:04,600
"Through their experiences on Earth, 
each spirit matures and grows.

157
00:19:04,850 --> 00:19:07,310
When the physical body dies...

158
00:19:07,560 --> 00:19:12,360
...the mature spirit, enriched by 
its life on Earth, returns to Gaia...

159
00:19:12,610 --> 00:19:15,280
...bringing with it the experiences...

160
00:19:16,280 --> 00:19:18,200
...enabling Gaia to live and grow. "

161
00:19:18,410 --> 00:19:19,950
It's my old diary.

162
00:19:20,410 --> 00:19:24,120
I wrote that 43 years ago, 
when I was the age you are now.

163
00:19:26,620 --> 00:19:27,710
Dr. Sid!

164
00:19:27,920 --> 00:19:31,710
Remember what happened to Galileo? 
They threw him in jail because...

165
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:34,960
...he said the Earth was not 
the center of the universe.

166
00:19:35,170 --> 00:19:37,180
That could happen to us.

167
00:19:37,380 --> 00:19:40,180
Our ideas are unpopular, Aki.

168
00:19:40,390 --> 00:19:43,560
If you have any notes or records 
that could be used against you...

169
00:19:43,760 --> 00:19:45,100
...destroy them.

170
00:19:45,560 --> 00:19:47,730
- Keep them up here. 
- Right.

171
00:19:47,730 --> 00:19:48,440
- Keep them up here. 
- Right.

172
00:19:48,640 --> 00:19:51,440
And stay away from your friend, the captain.

173
00:19:51,650 --> 00:19:55,150
He saves your life, you save his life, 
this leads to that.

174
00:19:55,400 --> 00:19:56,860
I was young once too, you know.

175
00:19:57,070 --> 00:19:59,990
Doctor, there is a war going on.

176
00:20:00,410 --> 00:20:02,870
No one's young anymore.

177
00:21:05,010 --> 00:21:06,640
Ladies and gentlemen of the council...

178
00:21:07,100 --> 00:21:09,180
...could you please explain why?

179
00:21:09,730 --> 00:21:11,850
Zeus was completed a month ago.

180
00:21:12,730 --> 00:21:16,980
If we attack the meteor with this, we will 
eliminate the Phantoms at their source.

181
00:21:17,190 --> 00:21:18,940
General Hein, calm down.

182
00:21:19,490 --> 00:21:21,150
At our last meeting, We voted 6 to 2...

183
00:21:21,360 --> 00:21:24,820
...to postpone using the Zeus cannon 
to attack the Leonid Meteor.

184
00:21:25,660 --> 00:21:28,330
We have re-convened today to vote 
on that very issue again.

185
00:21:28,540 --> 00:21:32,960
Now, I'd like to ask the director 
of the Bio-Etheric Center to speak.

186
00:21:33,170 --> 00:21:35,540
- Dr. Sid, please. 
- Thank you.

187
00:21:36,710 --> 00:21:39,840
As you all know, the Phantoms' nest 
is in the Leonid Meteor...

188
00:21:40,050 --> 00:21:42,550
...that landed here 34 years ago.

189
00:21:42,930 --> 00:21:47,510
What you see now are the records 
of every assault on the meteor to date.

190
00:21:47,720 --> 00:21:51,520
Physical attacks have had 
utterly no effect.

191
00:21:51,770 --> 00:21:55,730
This scene took place three months ago 
during a full-scale bombardment.

192
00:21:56,190 --> 00:22:00,070
Now please note the Phantoms outside 
the meteor are indeed destroyed.

193
00:22:00,360 --> 00:22:04,160
However, inside, many that 
were dormant come to life...

194
00:22:04,360 --> 00:22:08,740
...and as you see, 
overall Phantom density remains the same.

195
00:22:08,990 --> 00:22:11,700
The newly risen aliens 
respond to the attack...

196
00:22:11,950 --> 00:22:14,670
...by burrowing even 
deeper into the Earth.

197
00:22:14,870 --> 00:22:17,540
Now, this is very interesting to me Dr. Sid...

198
00:22:17,750 --> 00:22:20,840
...because we see 
the same thing during surgery...

199
00:22:21,050 --> 00:22:25,550
...when using bio-etheric lasers 
on Phantom particles, do we not?

200
00:22:25,930 --> 00:22:27,260
Yes, indeed we do.

201
00:22:27,470 --> 00:22:30,010
You see. the injured particles escape...

202
00:22:30,220 --> 00:22:33,390
...burying or digging themselves deeper 
into a patient's body.

203
00:22:33,600 --> 00:22:38,520
And when we increase the laser power 
to destroy these deeper particles...

204
00:22:38,900 --> 00:22:42,860
...we have had incidents resulting in 
further injury to a patient...

205
00:22:43,070 --> 00:22:44,900
...and in some cases...

206
00:22:45,110 --> 00:22:46,240
...death.

207
00:22:46,660 --> 00:22:48,530
And what exactly does that mean doctor?

208
00:22:48,780 --> 00:22:51,200
It means there's a very good chance...

209
00:22:51,410 --> 00:22:54,660
...the beam from the Zeus cannon 
will burn the Phantoms in the meteor.

210
00:22:54,960 --> 00:22:56,040
Exactly! Thank you.

211
00:22:56,250 --> 00:23:00,920
However, it also means that 
the beam energy may be too strong...

212
00:23:01,170 --> 00:23:02,590
...injuring the Earth.

213
00:23:02,800 --> 00:23:04,800
Injure the Earth?

214
00:23:05,170 --> 00:23:07,090
You mean the Gaia.

215
00:23:07,300 --> 00:23:10,260
- I mean... 
- You mean the spirit of the Earth.

216
00:23:11,970 --> 00:23:15,600
Yes, the spirit of the Earth.

217
00:23:16,270 --> 00:23:18,100
Did he say what I think he said?

218
00:23:18,310 --> 00:23:19,440
What are you doing?

219
00:23:19,650 --> 00:23:22,570
I know what I'm doing and 
whatever you do, keep your mouth shut.

220
00:23:22,780 --> 00:23:23,980
This is ridiculous.

221
00:23:24,280 --> 00:23:26,110
Doctor, with all due respect...

222
00:23:26,320 --> 00:23:29,570
...did you come here just to talk 
about some Gaia theory?

223
00:23:29,780 --> 00:23:32,450
To tell us that the planet is alive?

224
00:23:32,660 --> 00:23:34,250
That it has a spirit?

225
00:23:34,500 --> 00:23:37,250
That's a fairy tale doctor and I'm sorry, 
but we don't have time for that.

226
00:23:37,460 --> 00:23:40,130
It is not a fairy tale. It is true.

227
00:23:40,130 --> 00:23:40,170
It is not a fairy tale. It is true.

228
00:23:41,710 --> 00:23:45,710
Ahh.. Oh.. So if I point a gun 
at the Earth and fire...

229
00:23:46,010 --> 00:23:49,680
...I'm not just making a hole on the ground, 
I'm killing the planet.

230
00:23:49,890 --> 00:23:50,090
Dr. Sid, the Gaia theory 
has not been proven.

231
00:23:50,090 --> 00:23:52,010
Dr. Sid, the Gaia theory 
has not been proven.

232
00:23:52,220 --> 00:23:57,060
Even if Gaia does exist, won't we 
still have to remove the Phantoms?

233
00:23:57,310 --> 00:24:00,480
I think if there's any chance of success, 
we should take it.

234
00:24:00,690 --> 00:24:02,820
- Don't you agree? 
- Well, of course i do.

235
00:24:03,020 --> 00:24:05,480
But there is an alternative 
to the space cannon.

236
00:24:05,690 --> 00:24:06,820
Another method?

237
00:24:07,030 --> 00:24:10,490
- Yes. A means of disabling the Phantoms. 
- Please.

238
00:24:11,740 --> 00:24:15,830
As we know, the aliens display 
a distinct energy pattern.

239
00:24:16,750 --> 00:24:20,210
Now, it is a fact that 
two opposing bio-etheric waves...

240
00:24:20,460 --> 00:24:22,960
...placed one over the other 
will cancel each other out.

241
00:24:23,170 --> 00:24:26,460
It is theoretically possible 
to construct a wave pattern...

242
00:24:26,710 --> 00:24:28,800
...in direct opposition 
to the Phantom energy.

243
00:24:29,010 --> 00:24:32,180
We are currently assembling such 
a wave and are nearing completion.

244
00:24:32,390 --> 00:24:34,010
Members of the council...

245
00:24:34,220 --> 00:24:37,390
...gathering plants and animals...

246
00:24:37,600 --> 00:24:41,020
...from around the world to fight 
the Phantoms is utter nonsense.

247
00:24:41,690 --> 00:24:45,190
The Zeus cannon is a proven, 
effective weapon.

248
00:24:45,440 --> 00:24:48,110
It will kill Phantoms.

249
00:24:48,440 --> 00:24:51,320
Can we afford to wait 
for some crazy invention...

250
00:24:51,530 --> 00:24:55,830
...some army of 
touchy-feely plants and animals...

251
00:24:56,080 --> 00:24:59,040
...An invention that offers no solid evidence 
that it will destroy the aliens?

252
00:24:59,250 --> 00:25:00,410
There is evidence!

253
00:25:00,620 --> 00:25:02,920
Our partially completed energy wave...

254
00:25:03,170 --> 00:25:05,710
...has successfully stopped 
Phantom particles from spreading...

255
00:25:05,960 --> 00:25:08,420
...through a terminally-infected patient.

256
00:25:08,760 --> 00:25:11,800
Doctor, do you claim to have evidence 
that a terminal patient has been cured?

257
00:25:12,050 --> 00:25:15,180
Not cured. The wave is not complete.

258
00:25:15,390 --> 00:25:19,890
But we've succeeded in containing the 
particles safely inside the patient.

259
00:25:19,890 --> 00:25:19,930
But we've succeeded in containing the 
particles safely inside the patient.

260
00:25:20,730 --> 00:25:23,100
Where is the proof?

261
00:25:23,770 --> 00:25:24,360
Here.

262
00:25:24,360 --> 00:25:24,940
Here.

263
00:25:38,790 --> 00:25:42,290
You may have bought us some time Aki, 
but i wonder at what cost?

264
00:25:42,580 --> 00:25:45,830
Doctor, I can't keep hiding 
in the background while you protect me.

265
00:25:46,340 --> 00:25:49,050
I want what life I have left 
to mean something.

266
00:25:49,260 --> 00:25:52,680
Will you listen to me? When we find 
the seventh and eighth spirits...

267
00:25:52,930 --> 00:25:55,840
If we find them. 
What we need now is some luck.

268
00:25:56,100 --> 00:25:58,930
Luck has nothing to do with it.

269
00:25:59,140 --> 00:26:01,520
Faith and hard work, girl...

270
00:26:01,770 --> 00:26:05,270
...coz I'll be damned if 
you're going to die before me.

271
00:26:33,380 --> 00:26:36,720
The council decided to postpone 
firing the Zeus cannon.

272
00:26:37,010 --> 00:26:38,890
I guess I put on a good show.

273
00:26:39,140 --> 00:26:40,600
Mind if I tag along?

274
00:26:40,850 --> 00:26:42,810
You'll probably get bored.

275
00:26:55,650 --> 00:26:57,530
So, what are you doing?

276
00:27:00,410 --> 00:27:03,790
Oh, I see. You're giving me 
the silent treatment.

277
00:27:04,200 --> 00:27:07,370
I'm scanning the city 
for the seventh spirit.

278
00:27:19,510 --> 00:27:20,510
Hurry up, Neil.

279
00:27:20,800 --> 00:27:23,100
- Relax sergeant. Almost got it. 
- What do you think you're doing?

280
00:27:23,350 --> 00:27:25,560
We're just gonna strand them for a while.

281
00:27:26,390 --> 00:27:28,100
Hey, don't look at me. It was his idea.

282
00:27:28,310 --> 00:27:29,690
This was your idea?

283
00:27:29,940 --> 00:27:31,770
We're just helping the captain out a little.

284
00:27:32,020 --> 00:27:33,820
Yeah, come on Jane. 
Where's your sense of romance?

285
00:27:34,030 --> 00:27:35,900
You've seen how 
the captain looks at her.

286
00:27:35,900 --> 00:27:36,570
You've seen how 
the captain looks at her.

287
00:27:40,740 --> 00:27:42,530
It's amore, baby.

288
00:27:44,120 --> 00:27:45,790
What's going on?

289
00:27:46,040 --> 00:27:47,710
It's probably just a glitch.

290
00:27:48,460 --> 00:27:51,590
- Listen, Aki... 
- I'm still mad at you.

291
00:27:51,920 --> 00:27:53,880
- You're mad at me? 
- Leaving your helmet on.

292
00:27:54,170 --> 00:27:57,340
Not telling me who you were. 
That doesn't seem a little childish?

293
00:27:57,590 --> 00:28:01,800
Hey! Well, I was just a little upset when you just packed 
up and left for the Zeus Station without saying a word.

294
00:28:02,050 --> 00:28:05,100
- Well, now you know what was going on. Alright? 
- Yeah. Now I know.

295
00:28:05,350 --> 00:28:07,690
My operation had to be done 
in zero grav. Okay?

296
00:28:07,890 --> 00:28:08,940
Fine.

297
00:28:09,310 --> 00:28:12,190
And how about the fact that I was sent there 
on a job and you wouldn't even see me.

298
00:28:12,440 --> 00:28:14,860
I was probably helping Dr. Sid 
collect spirit waves.

299
00:28:15,070 --> 00:28:16,530
- Well, now I know. 
- So I'm sorry!

300
00:28:16,740 --> 00:28:19,410
Well, me too! So we're both sorry.

301
00:28:26,040 --> 00:28:27,910
So will you tell me about them?

302
00:28:28,120 --> 00:28:29,710
About what?

303
00:28:29,920 --> 00:28:32,210
About the spirits you've collected.

304
00:28:33,210 --> 00:28:36,710
I was infected by a Phantom 
during an experiment.

305
00:28:36,920 --> 00:28:40,260
- Normally, no one could have survived. 
- How did you?

306
00:28:40,470 --> 00:28:44,510
Dr. Sid created a membrane around 
the infection, keeping me alive.

307
00:28:44,720 --> 00:28:47,310
So the first spirit wave was me.

308
00:28:47,520 --> 00:28:50,190
- The second was a fish. 
- A fish?

309
00:28:50,440 --> 00:28:54,400
The third was a deer I found 
in a wildlife preserve outside Moscow.

310
00:28:55,110 --> 00:28:56,730
The fourth was a bird.

311
00:28:56,940 --> 00:29:01,030
Ever tried to track a sparrow 
from outer space? It's no fun.

312
00:29:01,240 --> 00:29:03,990
- What am I saying? You probably would love that. 
- You're right. I probably would.

313
00:29:04,200 --> 00:29:07,370
And then there was that plant 
I collected from Times Square.

314
00:29:07,580 --> 00:29:09,370
- I thought that was number six. 
- What?

315
00:29:09,580 --> 00:29:10,080
You skipped one.

316
00:29:13,920 --> 00:29:18,840
The fifth was a little girl dying 
in a hospital emergency room.

317
00:29:19,300 --> 00:29:22,590
I retrieved the sample 
in time, but she...

318
00:29:24,640 --> 00:29:29,770
I told her everything had a spirit: 
Dogs, cats, trees, little girls.

319
00:29:30,140 --> 00:29:31,600
Even the Earth.

320
00:29:32,140 --> 00:29:35,940
I told her that she wasn't dying 
just returning to the Earth's spirit...

321
00:29:36,150 --> 00:29:37,650
...to Gaia.

322
00:29:40,530 --> 00:29:44,450
She told me that she was ready to die.

323
00:29:47,870 --> 00:29:52,330
She said I didn't have to make up 
stories to make her feel better.

324
00:29:55,960 --> 00:29:58,500
Only 7 years old and ready to die.

325
00:29:58,960 --> 00:30:00,340
I'm sorry.

326
00:30:01,550 --> 00:30:05,970
I have work to do. I have to find 
the seventh and eighth spirits.

327
00:30:06,180 --> 00:30:08,850
Don't, please.

328
00:30:09,310 --> 00:30:11,930
You don't believe any of this, do you?

329
00:30:12,140 --> 00:30:14,350
I just don't know, Aki.

330
00:30:19,530 --> 00:30:21,690
Is this why you shut me out?

331
00:30:21,900 --> 00:30:23,700
You should have told me.

332
00:30:24,570 --> 00:30:27,700
I don't know how much time I have left.

333
00:30:28,660 --> 00:30:29,910
Who does?

334
00:30:35,330 --> 00:30:37,880
I better get back to scanning.

335
00:30:53,560 --> 00:30:54,850
Captain Edwards...

336
00:30:55,560 --> 00:30:59,860
...you extracted a Dr. Ross from 
Old New York several days ago did you not?

337
00:31:00,070 --> 00:31:03,360
- Yes, sir. 
- What were your impressions of Dr. Ross?

338
00:31:03,690 --> 00:31:07,030
She seemed very capable and determined, sir.

339
00:31:07,240 --> 00:31:11,030
You and the Deep Eyes are being 
temporarily reassigned.

340
00:31:11,580 --> 00:31:14,830
You will guard Dr. Ross 
when she reenters the wasteland.

341
00:31:14,080 --> 00:31:18,380
- Understood, sir. 
- You don't understand yet, captain.

342
00:31:18,750 --> 00:31:22,920
Report any aberrant behavior 
in Dr. Ross to the major immediately.

343
00:31:23,130 --> 00:31:24,380
Aberrant behavior sir?

344
00:31:24,590 --> 00:31:29,760
The woman carries an alien infestation, captain. 
We don't know what it may be doing to her.

345
00:31:29,970 --> 00:31:32,390
The alien presence could be affecting her judgment.

346
00:31:32,600 --> 00:31:35,600
They may be manipulating the doctor 
for their very own purposes.

347
00:31:35,890 --> 00:31:39,810
Is the general suggesting 
that Dr. Ross is a spy?

348
00:31:40,270 --> 00:31:44,440
The general is wondering why 
he's explaining himself to a captain.

349
00:31:44,740 --> 00:31:47,570
She's had prolonged exposure 
to Phantom tissue.

350
00:31:47,860 --> 00:31:50,490
If this begins to manifest itself in any way...

351
00:31:50,700 --> 00:31:55,500
...Dr. Ross is to be placed under arrest 
and transported here for observation.

352
00:31:56,870 --> 00:31:59,960
It is, in fact, for her own good, captain.

353
00:32:00,210 --> 00:32:01,290
Of course, sir.

354
00:32:09,340 --> 00:32:13,810
Major, send some of our men 
to keep an eye on the good captain.

355
00:33:49,280 --> 00:33:52,950
I'm convinced that these dreams 
are some form of communication.

356
00:33:53,160 --> 00:33:55,160
Their message still eludes me...

357
00:33:55,370 --> 00:33:59,830
...but they're coming faster now 
and that can only mean one thing.

358
00:34:00,290 --> 00:34:03,250
The Phantoms inside me are beginning to win.

359
00:34:03,460 --> 00:34:06,590
Our target is 50 klicks west of Tucson.

360
00:34:07,290 --> 00:34:08,340
- Roger. 
- Phantom concentration?

361
00:34:08,550 --> 00:34:10,960
Not good. We've got big metas everywhere.

362
00:34:11,170 --> 00:34:13,010
So it's gonna be a real picnic.

363
00:34:13,220 --> 00:34:17,010
Stick close to me. No heroics today. Okay? 
Everything by the book.

364
00:34:17,220 --> 00:34:19,060
By the book. Right.

365
00:34:25,650 --> 00:34:29,150
If we drop energy buoys here, 
here and here...

366
00:34:29,400 --> 00:34:31,190
...we should be able to 
land, acquire the target,

367
00:34:31,190 --> 00:34:33,240
and get out before the Phantoms 
even know we were there.

368
00:34:33,450 --> 00:34:35,530
And the buoys will attract the Phantoms?

369
00:34:35,740 --> 00:34:37,700
- Yeah. 
- For a while.

370
00:34:47,250 --> 00:34:50,380
So you're from the 307th's right? 
Under General Hein?

371
00:34:50,590 --> 00:34:54,720
Ever done wasteland recon before? 
It can get pretty ugly.

372
00:35:21,330 --> 00:35:26,710
Captain, rendezvous for evac at 
vector 6, coordinate 279.

373
00:35:27,790 --> 00:35:30,380
Roger that. Stay alert for hostiles.

374
00:35:48,650 --> 00:35:50,900
Looks like they've taken the bait.

375
00:36:06,450 --> 00:36:09,620
The seventh spirit should be 
just beyond that line of wreckage.

376
00:36:09,830 --> 00:36:12,710
I don't see how any living thing 
could survive out here?

377
00:36:12,920 --> 00:36:15,170
We'll find out soon enough.

378
00:36:16,920 --> 00:36:19,680
This was the Phantom Cleansing Mission.

379
00:36:19,930 --> 00:36:22,430
It was supposed to end the war.

380
00:36:25,020 --> 00:36:27,600
My father's in here somewhere.

381
00:36:30,650 --> 00:36:31,730
All right.

382
00:36:32,400 --> 00:36:34,190
Let's move out, people.

383
00:36:50,370 --> 00:36:51,630
I'll be damned.

384
00:36:51,830 --> 00:36:52,920
A survivor.

385
00:36:54,210 --> 00:36:55,710
What's it doing out here?

386
00:36:55,920 --> 00:36:57,800
Hoping for life to return.

387
00:36:59,260 --> 00:37:01,010
Is that our spirit, doc?

388
00:37:02,970 --> 00:37:04,010
No.

389
00:37:18,190 --> 00:37:19,900
We're closing in on the life form.

390
00:37:20,110 --> 00:37:24,070
- Distance? 
- Hard to say. We're very close.

391
00:37:24,570 --> 00:37:26,620
I don't see anything.

392
00:37:32,040 --> 00:37:35,540
- You're not gonna tell me it's him? 
- That's impossible.

393
00:37:43,930 --> 00:37:45,720
It's not the soldier. It's his ovo-pac.

394
00:37:45,930 --> 00:37:49,850
How do you explain that? The pacs power 
our weapons, the barrier cities...

395
00:37:50,060 --> 00:37:51,810
I mean it's just bio-etheric energy.

396
00:37:52,020 --> 00:37:55,440
And to create that energy we use 
living tissue. Single-cell organisms.

397
00:37:55,650 --> 00:37:58,440
- You're telling me his backpack is the seventh spirit? 
- Yes.

398
00:37:58,650 --> 00:38:00,530
We have incoming. Captain? Do you read me?

399
00:38:00,740 --> 00:38:01,820
- Captain? 
- What? Say again?

400
00:38:02,110 --> 00:38:03,950
You read me captain? We have incoming.

401
00:38:04,200 --> 00:38:06,070
Ryan, get the soldier's pac.

402
00:38:23,590 --> 00:38:25,800
I need a hand! Sarge!

403
00:38:30,020 --> 00:38:33,100
- Those buoys? They're not working. 
- Yeah.

404
00:38:36,020 --> 00:38:38,820
- Are you all right? 
- Of course I am.

405
00:38:39,070 --> 00:38:40,780
Let's get the hell out of here!

406
00:38:44,450 --> 00:38:46,490
Something's not right. 
This shouldn't be happening.

407
00:38:46,700 --> 00:38:48,990
Something's attracting them.

408
00:38:49,990 --> 00:38:51,080
Aki!

409
00:38:55,540 --> 00:38:59,460
- They're right on us, sir. Closing in fast! 
- Jane, take the lead.

410
00:39:14,230 --> 00:39:15,480
Fire in the hole!

411
00:39:28,200 --> 00:39:29,910
Get us out of here, Neil.

412
00:39:30,530 --> 00:39:32,580
- Sir, I would love to, but... 
- Just do it!

413
00:39:58,600 --> 00:39:59,850
- Sir? 
- It's okay, that's it.

414
00:40:01,520 --> 00:40:03,230
That doesn't look good, captain.

415
00:40:03,900 --> 00:40:05,690
We have to get her to a hospital.

416
00:40:05,900 --> 00:40:09,490
- You have your orders, sir. 
- What the hell is going on here?

417
00:40:09,740 --> 00:40:13,450
Dr. Ross is to be taken into custody now, sir.

418
00:40:17,750 --> 00:40:19,710
Lower your weapons. That's an order!

419
00:40:19,960 --> 00:40:21,920
Sir. We have no choice, 
but to relieve you of your command.

420
00:40:22,170 --> 00:40:24,630
I won't let you do this soldier. 
You'll gonna have to shoot me.

421
00:40:24,920 --> 00:40:26,460
Stand down, captain!

422
00:41:50,340 --> 00:41:52,430
Hang on, everyone!

423
00:41:57,140 --> 00:42:01,230
That's enough. 
Hands where I can see them. Everyone now!

424
00:42:11,950 --> 00:42:13,490
Deep Eyes, hard to starboard!

425
00:42:25,290 --> 00:42:27,590
Neil, get us back to New York, fast!

426
00:42:38,470 --> 00:42:41,470
The Deep Eyes are returning 
from the wasteland, sir.

427
00:42:41,680 --> 00:42:43,270
Apparently, there was an incident.

428
00:42:43,560 --> 00:42:46,350
It would seem the Phantoms 
were attracted to Dr. Ross.

429
00:42:46,600 --> 00:42:49,820
The crew barely escaped with their lives.

430
00:42:50,020 --> 00:42:52,530
And sir, Captain Edwards is still in command.

431
00:42:52,740 --> 00:42:54,240
Issue an order.

432
00:42:54,450 --> 00:42:57,410
I want Edwards and Dr. Ross 
placed under arrest.

433
00:42:57,620 --> 00:43:00,910
All research materials pertaining 
to Dr. Sid's wave theory...

434
00:43:01,120 --> 00:43:02,750
...are to be confiscated immediately.

435
00:43:02,950 --> 00:43:05,870
That might not go over 
too well with the council, sir.

436
00:43:06,080 --> 00:43:08,500
What a tragedy that would be.

437
00:43:08,710 --> 00:43:13,010
This is perfect, major. 
The good captain has opened the door for us.

438
00:43:13,800 --> 00:43:16,220
By tomorrow morning, 
the council will be at our feet...

439
00:43:16,430 --> 00:43:19,850
...thanking us for exposing 
the traitors and imploring us...

440
00:43:20,050 --> 00:43:22,180
...to save them from the Phantoms.

441
00:43:26,850 --> 00:43:28,440
How is she, doctor?

442
00:43:29,230 --> 00:43:32,690
- She is dying. 
- There must be something you can do.

443
00:43:32,980 --> 00:43:35,280
Aki is fighting with 
only six of the eight spirits.

444
00:43:35,490 --> 00:43:38,570
We'll have to implant the seventh 
directly into her chest plate.

445
00:43:38,780 --> 00:43:41,240
It took a bullet. 
I think it might be damaged.

446
00:43:41,700 --> 00:43:43,620
We have to repair this panel quickly.

447
00:43:44,700 --> 00:43:49,380
Her vital signs are dropping. 
Aki is slipping away from us.

448
00:43:50,080 --> 00:43:54,630
She needs a sympathetic spirit 
to help hold her in this world.

449
00:43:54,840 --> 00:43:59,510
And I can think of no spirit better suited 
for that task than yours, captain.

450
00:43:59,760 --> 00:44:03,470
- I don't understand. 
- You don't have to understand.

451
00:44:03,930 --> 00:44:05,890
You just be with her now.

452
00:44:07,020 --> 00:44:09,100
You keep her here with us.

453
00:45:01,200 --> 00:45:03,530
Aki? Where are we?

454
00:45:03,740 --> 00:45:05,620
On an alien planet.

455
00:45:05,830 --> 00:45:07,450
How is that possible?

456
00:45:09,080 --> 00:45:11,250
I'm not entirely sure.

457
00:45:11,460 --> 00:45:12,960
You seem pretty calm.

458
00:45:13,170 --> 00:45:16,420
I've been having this dream 
every night for months.

459
00:45:16,630 --> 00:45:17,670
Dream?

460
00:45:18,260 --> 00:45:20,380
Well, whatever it is.

461
00:45:22,300 --> 00:45:24,800
You're really here, aren't you?

462
00:45:26,720 --> 00:45:27,970
What's happening to me?

463
00:45:28,270 --> 00:45:33,020
Dr. Sid is implanting the seventh spirit 
directly into your body.

464
00:45:33,230 --> 00:45:35,940
Then you're my spiritual support.

465
00:45:36,150 --> 00:45:38,860
Gray, how sweet of you.

466
00:45:39,190 --> 00:45:43,450
Look, I don't think you realize 
how serious this situation is.

467
00:45:46,700 --> 00:45:49,200
Something you should see here, sir.

468
00:45:56,920 --> 00:45:59,170
And I am watching what, major?

469
00:45:59,380 --> 00:46:02,840
It seems Dr. Ross has been recording her dreams.

470
00:46:03,050 --> 00:46:05,640
And why would I be interested in...

471
00:46:07,050 --> 00:46:08,310
...her dreams?

472
00:46:08,760 --> 00:46:10,980
This is it. This is our evidence.

473
00:46:11,180 --> 00:46:13,980
She's under the influence of the Phantoms.

474
00:46:18,570 --> 00:46:23,070
Dr. Ross' dreams should be all the council needs 
to authorize the firing of the Zeus cannon.

475
00:46:23,280 --> 00:46:26,660
The council is content to hide 
powering inside this barrier...

476
00:46:26,870 --> 00:46:29,410
...while the world dies a little more every day.

477
00:46:29,620 --> 00:46:32,410
I believe they need a push 
in the right direction, major.

478
00:46:32,620 --> 00:46:35,370
Get together a group of your most trusted men.

479
00:47:27,220 --> 00:47:29,350
What are they doing. 
Why are they staring at us?

480
00:47:29,550 --> 00:47:31,100
Not at us.

481
00:48:21,690 --> 00:48:23,650
Welcome back, captain.

482
00:48:26,400 --> 00:48:27,610
Is it over?

483
00:48:28,530 --> 00:48:30,200
How is she, doctor?

484
00:48:30,410 --> 00:48:32,620
She's gonna be fine. 
But this is only temporary.

485
00:48:32,870 --> 00:48:36,410
We'll need to find the eighth 
and final spirit to cure her.

486
00:48:39,540 --> 00:48:42,040
Aki, can you hear me?

487
00:48:44,380 --> 00:48:46,010
I finished it.

488
00:48:46,210 --> 00:48:48,050
I know what it means.

489
00:48:48,260 --> 00:48:51,010
I know what the Phantoms really are.

490
00:48:52,220 --> 00:48:55,510
Nobody move! You're all under arrest!

491
00:49:06,440 --> 00:49:07,860
We have them, sir.

492
00:49:09,150 --> 00:49:10,240
Sir?

493
00:49:10,780 --> 00:49:12,990
My wife and daughter...

494
00:49:15,160 --> 00:49:19,830
...were killed by Phantoms in the 
San Francisco Barrier City was attacked.

495
00:49:20,040 --> 00:49:22,000
Did I ever tell you that?

496
00:49:24,500 --> 00:49:28,300
I try to imagine what.. 
what that must have been like...

497
00:49:28,510 --> 00:49:32,760
...seeing everyone around you 
fall over dead for no apparent reason.

498
00:49:34,010 --> 00:49:37,970
And then, at the end, 
feeling something next to you...

499
00:49:38,390 --> 00:49:39,680
...invisible...

500
00:49:40,430 --> 00:49:41,770
...touching you...

501
00:49:42,980 --> 00:49:45,520
...reaching inside your body...

502
00:49:47,900 --> 00:49:50,070
You've lost family, haven't you?

503
00:49:50,530 --> 00:49:51,740
Yes, sir.

504
00:49:52,240 --> 00:49:54,240
That's why I trust you.

505
00:49:55,240 --> 00:49:56,530
All of you.

506
00:49:56,870 --> 00:49:59,580
You know what must be done.

507
00:50:07,000 --> 00:50:09,260
Security override.

508
00:50:09,550 --> 00:50:12,220
Perimeter breached.

509
00:50:13,760 --> 00:50:16,050
Major, arrest these men.

510
00:50:16,640 --> 00:50:19,640
- Take it easy. 
- Stand up. Go.

511
00:50:19,850 --> 00:50:23,600
You are relieved of your post. 
Don't ask any questions.

512
00:50:25,480 --> 00:50:27,230
Reduce power to Sector 31.

513
00:50:27,440 --> 00:50:29,440
Sir, you do realize that the Phantoms...

514
00:50:29,690 --> 00:50:31,070
What I realize, major...

515
00:50:31,280 --> 00:50:35,240
...is that we must force the council 
to take action against the enemy.

516
00:50:41,700 --> 00:50:44,960
25% of energy pipe alpha redirected.

517
00:50:45,750 --> 00:50:48,670
Lowering power output to Sector 31.

518
00:50:49,800 --> 00:50:52,920
Barrier breached in Sector 31, general. 
They're coming through now.

519
00:50:53,090 --> 00:50:56,300
Oh I think we can easily handle 
a few Phantoms in a contained space.

520
00:50:57,260 --> 00:51:02,180
Relax, major. When this night's over, 
you're going to be a hero.

521
00:51:04,480 --> 00:51:07,560
- Aki, I don't think... 
- You were in my dream, Gray. You saw it.

522
00:51:07,770 --> 00:51:10,150
That's just it. I'm not sure what I saw. 
How can you be?

523
00:51:10,400 --> 00:51:12,740
Captain, please, let her continue.

524
00:51:12,940 --> 00:51:16,740
Alright. Why do you think 
we've never been able to determine...

525
00:51:16,950 --> 00:51:21,120
...a relationship between the human-sized Phantoms 
and the giant ones roaming the wastelands?

526
00:51:21,540 --> 00:51:25,080
Excuse me, doc, 
but what friggin' relationship?

527
00:51:25,290 --> 00:51:29,750
I mean you got your human-sized Phantoms, 
and your creepy caterpillary Phantoms...

528
00:51:29,960 --> 00:51:32,510
...and your flying Phantoms 
and let's not forget my personal favorite...

529
00:51:32,760 --> 00:51:34,380
...the big, fat, giant Phantoms.

530
00:51:34,720 --> 00:51:35,720
Down, boy.

531
00:51:35,930 --> 00:51:36,130
He's right. If you've spent as much time 
in the field as we had...

532
00:51:36,130 --> 00:51:38,550
He's right. If you've spent as much time 
in the field as we had...

533
00:51:38,760 --> 00:51:42,260
...you know there is no relationship. 
It's like a zoo out there.

534
00:51:42,470 --> 00:51:46,140
Precisely. I think the giant ones are 
like our whales or elephants.

535
00:51:46,350 --> 00:51:50,650
But why would an invading army bring 
a bunch of whales and elephants along for the ride?

536
00:51:50,900 --> 00:51:53,650
Unless their ship was kind of 
a crazy Noah's Ark?

537
00:51:54,240 --> 00:51:56,610
We have always assumed that the meteor...

538
00:51:56,860 --> 00:52:00,030
...was intended as a form of transportation. 
Perhaps it wasn't.

539
00:52:00,700 --> 00:52:03,540
The meteor is a chunk of their planet 
that got thrown into space...

540
00:52:03,740 --> 00:52:04,910
...when they destroyed their world.

541
00:52:05,160 --> 00:52:09,630
But how could they survive the trip 
across outer space on a hunk of rock?

542
00:52:09,830 --> 00:52:11,340
They didn't.

543
00:52:15,130 --> 00:52:17,760
Oh. This is all beginning to 
make a creepy kind of sense.

544
00:52:18,010 --> 00:52:19,470
What do you think about all this, captain?

545
00:52:20,010 --> 00:52:23,680
I think that explains why we never had a chance.

546
00:52:23,970 --> 00:52:27,480
All our strategies are based on one assumption:

547
00:52:27,770 --> 00:52:30,690
That we were fighting alien invaders.

548
00:52:30,900 --> 00:52:33,730
Think of the dream, Gray. How they died.

549
00:52:33,940 --> 00:52:36,780
Since then, all they've known is suffering.

550
00:52:36,990 --> 00:52:38,860
They're not an invading army.

551
00:52:39,070 --> 00:52:40,780
They're ghosts.

552
00:52:42,620 --> 00:52:43,870
How many Phantoms?

553
00:52:44,120 --> 00:52:45,910
More than enough to convince the council, sir.

554
00:52:46,160 --> 00:52:49,540
Excellent. Sound an alert. Send 
a squad out to eliminate them.

555
00:52:49,540 --> 00:52:50,460
Yes sir.

556
00:52:50,710 --> 00:52:53,250
Alert status. Full deployment.

557
00:52:53,500 --> 00:52:55,210
Sir. I have numerous Phantom contacts!

558
00:52:55,460 --> 00:52:56,920
Well, of course you do.

559
00:52:57,130 --> 00:52:59,970
Outside of Sector 31, sir. 
And moving at incredible speed.

560
00:53:00,180 --> 00:53:01,970
Major, What the hell is going on here?

561
00:53:02,180 --> 00:53:03,550
They're in the pipes.

562
00:53:03,760 --> 00:53:06,310
They're moving with the bio-etheric energy flow.

563
00:53:06,560 --> 00:53:10,440
That's impossible. No living thing 
could survive in those pipes.

564
00:53:10,940 --> 00:53:14,980
Well, we've got a big one heading this way. 
Meta class, sir.

565
00:53:22,360 --> 00:53:23,740
Oh, my God.

566
00:53:24,450 --> 00:53:25,740
Hold your fire!

567
00:54:12,460 --> 00:54:14,080
What have I done?

568
00:54:35,230 --> 00:54:39,480
Come on, Neil. We need to find a way out. 
You're our man. Think.

569
00:54:39,730 --> 00:54:43,570
Captain, these walls are titanium alloy 
and the bars are pulse-sonic lasers.

570
00:54:43,820 --> 00:54:46,370
I mean it's not like I can just 
wave a magic wand and...

571
00:54:46,370 --> 00:54:47,200
I mean it's not like I can just 
wave a magic wand and...

572
00:54:50,290 --> 00:54:53,040
- Wow! Neil, I'm impressed. 
- That makes two of us.

573
00:54:53,250 --> 00:54:56,290
Proceed to the nearest evacuation facility.

574
00:54:56,960 --> 00:54:58,960
Proceed to the nearest evacuation facility.

575
00:54:59,210 --> 00:55:02,590
I think we should proceed 
to the nearest evacuation facility.

576
00:55:27,360 --> 00:55:29,990
- Here they come. 
- But the others! Dr. Sid!

577
00:55:30,200 --> 00:55:32,490
Deep Eyes'll take care of him. 
Come on.

578
00:55:39,960 --> 00:55:42,090
What's happening. Why can we see them now?

579
00:55:42,340 --> 00:55:45,670
They must be carrying a residual charge 
from passing through the barrier.

580
00:55:50,600 --> 00:55:51,890
Behind you!

581
00:56:53,990 --> 00:56:55,580
All aboard, captain!

582
00:58:03,440 --> 00:58:04,480
We need to find my ship.

583
00:58:04,690 --> 00:58:07,360
If it was towed inside the city, 
it would be in the military hangar.

584
00:58:07,570 --> 00:58:09,320
That's a big "if. "

585
00:58:18,290 --> 00:58:19,490
Look out!

586
00:58:27,420 --> 00:58:29,510
- Get us onto the platform. 
- You got it.

587
00:58:47,440 --> 00:58:49,320
Okay, now what?

588
00:58:49,530 --> 00:58:51,320
We're going through the station.

589
00:58:51,530 --> 00:58:53,110
- What? 
- Captain, with all due respect...

590
00:58:53,320 --> 00:58:55,360
- Excuse me, captain. 
- The station.

591
00:58:55,570 --> 00:58:57,070
We're going through it.

592
00:58:57,320 --> 00:58:58,780
It's the only way.

593
00:58:59,160 --> 00:59:02,620
So I gather this will be 
somewhat of a rough ride?

594
00:59:02,830 --> 00:59:05,330
Doc, you've got a talent for understatement.

595
00:59:05,330 --> 00:59:05,370
Doc, you've got a talent for understatement.

596
00:59:05,580 --> 00:59:06,000
Hang on, everybody!

597
00:59:06,000 --> 00:59:07,080
Hang on, everybody!

598
00:59:31,900 --> 00:59:32,940
Doc?

599
00:59:37,570 --> 00:59:38,740
Interesting.

600
00:59:39,320 --> 00:59:41,580
- Anybody hurt? 
- Captain.

601
00:59:45,960 --> 00:59:48,420
Oh, God. Talk to me, sarge.

602
00:59:48,920 --> 00:59:49,960
Ouch!

603
00:59:50,170 --> 00:59:51,500
- Give me a hand, Jane. 
- Right.

604
00:59:51,710 --> 00:59:55,800
No wait! We're risking further injury. 
We need the proper tools to cut him out.

605
00:59:56,010 --> 00:59:57,300
They're in my ship.

606
00:59:58,720 --> 01:00:02,180
- No. No, doc. No drugs. 
- Captain?

607
01:00:02,390 --> 01:00:03,640
You heard the man.

608
01:00:04,350 --> 01:00:05,930
We'll find the ship and be back for you.

609
01:00:06,180 --> 01:00:07,940
- I'll stay with him. 
- Me too.

610
01:00:08,150 --> 01:00:09,730
Nobody's staying.

611
01:00:10,940 --> 01:00:12,860
- Just give me a gun. 
- You got it.

612
01:00:13,070 --> 01:00:15,610
Give him a weapon. Do it!

613
01:00:18,110 --> 01:00:19,910
We'll be back for you, sergeant.

614
01:00:20,240 --> 01:00:21,330
You hear me?

615
01:00:21,620 --> 01:00:24,830
I hear you, captain. 
Now, get out of here.

616
01:00:25,330 --> 01:00:26,660
Let's move out.

617
01:01:17,670 --> 01:01:20,010
A quad-axle ATV. This is good.

618
01:01:20,260 --> 01:01:24,300
It can be used to retrieve Ryan 
and transport him safely here.

619
01:01:24,510 --> 01:01:27,680
However, we'll need to replace 
these spent fuel cells.

620
01:01:27,970 --> 01:01:30,640
There could be some live ovo-pacs in the hangar.

621
01:01:30,850 --> 01:01:33,810
Alright. Jane, check the hangar. 
Neil, get us ready for takeoff.

622
01:01:34,020 --> 01:01:35,940
Aki and Dr. Sid, prep the Quatro.

623
01:01:36,150 --> 01:01:38,440
I'll go to the tower and rotate the airtray.

624
01:01:38,650 --> 01:01:43,320
This city may be lost, but we are not. 
Let's do this thing and get the hell out of here.

625
01:01:55,210 --> 01:01:56,290
Gray, be careful.

626
01:01:56,500 --> 01:01:57,710
You too.

627
01:02:40,170 --> 01:02:41,260
Oh, yeah.

628
01:02:56,940 --> 01:02:58,440
Neil, do you read me?

629
01:02:58,690 --> 01:03:00,190
Loud and clear, captain.

630
01:03:00,440 --> 01:03:02,240
This baby'll fly itself.

631
01:03:09,830 --> 01:03:11,120
Flight path is set.

632
01:03:11,330 --> 01:03:12,790
Beginning rotation.

633
01:03:16,330 --> 01:03:18,540
Stop the airtray. We have a problem.

634
01:03:18,750 --> 01:03:21,340
I'm reading an impound tractor 
attached probably to the ship.

635
01:03:21,550 --> 01:03:23,800
Can you disengage it from the cockpit?

636
01:03:24,010 --> 01:03:26,890
No sir. Permission to go outside 
and detach the coupling.

637
01:03:27,550 --> 01:03:28,640
Do it.

638
01:03:40,190 --> 01:03:41,690
There's the problem.

639
01:03:50,620 --> 01:03:53,120
The controls are locked, naturally.

640
01:03:56,040 --> 01:03:59,460
Jane, let me ask you something. 
You think we're gonna get out of here alive?

641
01:03:59,710 --> 01:04:01,500
I mean I wonder if anybody else has gotten out.

642
01:04:02,050 --> 01:04:04,260
You think anyone's made it this far? Huh?

643
01:04:04,800 --> 01:04:07,720
You think this eighth-spirit stuff 
is really gonna work against the Phantoms?

644
01:04:07,930 --> 01:04:10,140
I mean what if it's all a bunch of mumbo-jumbo?

645
01:04:12,350 --> 01:04:16,270
Jane, do you mind if we stop talking? 
I'm trying to concentrate here.

646
01:04:28,660 --> 01:04:30,410
What's happening down there?

647
01:04:30,660 --> 01:04:33,160
Nothing we can't handle.

648
01:04:45,090 --> 01:04:48,170
- Neil, what's your status? 
- Almost there.

649
01:04:48,510 --> 01:04:50,050
I want you two back inside.

650
01:04:50,260 --> 01:04:54,010
We're fine, sir. Jane is negotiating 
with extreme prejudice.

651
01:04:54,220 --> 01:04:55,470
Talk to me, Jane.

652
01:04:57,060 --> 01:04:59,140
No problem here, captain.

653
01:05:04,650 --> 01:05:07,280
Yes! Captain, we are good to go.

654
01:05:47,360 --> 01:05:49,070
Jane, get out of there.

655
01:05:49,400 --> 01:05:52,530
Get out of there now! Go! Jane!

656
01:05:52,740 --> 01:05:54,700
Get the hell out of there!

657
01:06:22,020 --> 01:06:24,730
The shield is powered and ready.

658
01:06:24,940 --> 01:06:26,310
- Where are you going? 
- To the cockpit.

659
01:06:26,520 --> 01:06:29,610
The ship is set on autopilot. 
We're in countdown to liftoff.

660
01:06:29,860 --> 01:06:33,200
No, wait. It's too dangerous. Aki!

661
01:06:57,100 --> 01:06:59,310
Over here, you son of a bitch!

662
01:08:26,140 --> 01:08:28,650
Gray, do you read me? 
What's happening?

663
01:08:28,900 --> 01:08:31,060
You and Sid are getting 
out of here now.

664
01:08:31,310 --> 01:08:34,480
- No! We can't just leave everyone. 
- Everyone's dead!

665
01:08:34,730 --> 01:08:38,610
- I'm not leaving without you. 
- I'm sorry, but you don't have a choice.

666
01:08:40,700 --> 01:08:42,030
Goodbye, Aki.

667
01:09:20,740 --> 01:09:22,820
Gray, come on!

668
01:11:27,070 --> 01:11:28,450
I just...

669
01:11:30,120 --> 01:11:33,410
I wish I could believe they were in a better place.

670
01:13:43,130 --> 01:13:45,000
I enlarged the scanning perimeter...

671
01:13:45,210 --> 01:13:48,010
...to include an area that 
we had previously overlooked.

672
01:13:48,210 --> 01:13:50,010
The impact crater.

673
01:13:51,050 --> 01:13:53,090
That's a strange place to find the eighth spirit.

674
01:13:53,300 --> 01:13:54,930
Yes, really quite astonishing.

675
01:13:55,140 --> 01:13:57,470
But nothing could survive in there except Phantoms.

676
01:13:57,680 --> 01:13:58,810
Precisely.

677
01:13:59,140 --> 01:14:02,310
Which suggests that 
the eighth spirit is a Phantom spirit.

678
01:14:02,520 --> 01:14:05,730
I can't explain it at the moment, 
but once we get down there...

679
01:14:05,940 --> 01:14:09,240
- ... you will understand... 
- Wait, doctor. That's a one-way trip.

680
01:14:09,440 --> 01:14:12,530
Yes, I expected that's how 
you would evaluate our chances.

681
01:14:12,780 --> 01:14:14,200
Well, am I wrong?

682
01:14:14,410 --> 01:14:15,740
No, I agree. We probably...

683
01:14:15,990 --> 01:14:19,200
...won't live long enough to extract 
the eighth spirit from the crater.

684
01:14:19,410 --> 01:14:20,080
Then why should we even try it?

685
01:14:21,210 --> 01:14:23,290
Because we don't need to extract the eighth spirit.

686
01:14:23,500 --> 01:14:25,290
If we can't bring the final spirit here...

687
01:14:25,500 --> 01:14:28,050
...we can go there and complete 
the wave inside the crater.

688
01:14:28,250 --> 01:14:29,670
Yes, exactly.

689
01:14:29,880 --> 01:14:31,840
And how do we do that, exactly?

690
01:14:32,260 --> 01:14:34,140
I can construct a device that...

691
01:14:34,340 --> 01:14:38,640
...would attach to Aki's chest plate 
to gather the eighth spirit and then...

692
01:14:39,810 --> 01:14:40,930
And then what?

693
01:14:41,270 --> 01:14:44,440
And then we wait 
and see what happens.

694
01:14:45,100 --> 01:14:46,190
That's it?

695
01:14:46,860 --> 01:14:49,780
- That's your plan? We wait and see what happens? 
- Yes.

696
01:14:51,530 --> 01:14:54,360
Oh, good. Well, I got my own plan.

697
01:14:54,820 --> 01:14:56,450
We keep scanning the surface from orbit...

698
01:14:56,700 --> 01:14:59,120
- and maybe we'll find a 
compatible spirit somewhere else.

699
01:14:59,120 --> 01:14:59,410
Aki?

700
01:15:00,950 --> 01:15:02,830
I say we go in.

701
01:15:32,440 --> 01:15:35,150
What caused the barrier 
to fail, General Hein?

702
01:15:36,950 --> 01:15:38,780
I'm afraid it was 
only a matter of time...

703
01:15:38,990 --> 01:15:42,200
...before the Phantoms developed 
an immunity to our barriers.

704
01:15:42,620 --> 01:15:45,080
But I am relieved to see that you 
and the rest of the council...

705
01:15:45,290 --> 01:15:48,790
...were able to evacuate to Houston without incident.

706
01:15:49,000 --> 01:15:51,710
It was a terrible loss suffered this evening.

707
01:15:51,920 --> 01:15:54,970
The council has reconsidered 
your proposal to fire the Zeus cannon.

708
01:15:55,170 --> 01:15:56,380
I see.

709
01:15:56,760 --> 01:15:58,970
We are transmitting the access codes to you now.

710
01:16:00,970 --> 01:16:02,270
And, general...

711
01:16:03,680 --> 01:16:05,850
...best of luck to us all.

712
01:16:08,850 --> 01:16:10,360
Prepare to fire the cannon.

713
01:16:10,610 --> 01:16:11,690
The target, sir?

714
01:16:13,400 --> 01:16:15,190
The Phantom crater.

715
01:16:41,850 --> 01:16:46,180
Preparing to drop in three, two, one.

716
01:16:50,730 --> 01:16:52,440
Powering the shield.

717
01:16:55,400 --> 01:16:57,190
Okay, we're over the meteor.

718
01:16:57,400 --> 01:16:58,900
Do you have it in sight, doctor?

719
01:16:59,910 --> 01:17:02,450
There are so many of them.

720
01:17:04,370 --> 01:17:05,410
Wait.

721
01:17:05,620 --> 01:17:09,750
Yes! I'm tracking the eighth spirit 
moving along the crater's surface.

722
01:17:10,330 --> 01:17:13,460
All right. Now let's take a closer look.

723
01:17:53,670 --> 01:17:55,380
Ready to fire in three minutes.

724
01:17:55,590 --> 01:17:59,380
Ovo-pacs at maximum. 
Transferring plasma flow to auto.

725
01:17:59,880 --> 01:18:01,880
Counter-thrusters are engaged.

726
01:18:02,090 --> 01:18:04,930
Lox flow de-coupled. Status is green.

727
01:18:05,140 --> 01:18:08,930
We have something on radar 
over the impact site, sir.

728
01:18:11,100 --> 01:18:12,440
It's her.

729
01:18:12,690 --> 01:18:13,810
Sir?

730
01:18:14,020 --> 01:18:16,520
Just a traitor under 
the influence of the enemy.

731
01:18:16,730 --> 01:18:18,480
Continue the countdown.

732
01:18:18,690 --> 01:18:21,700
We'll take them all out at the same time.

733
01:18:25,070 --> 01:18:29,080
We're closing on the Phantom. 
Contact in 30 seconds.

734
01:18:30,410 --> 01:18:31,830
Target locked.

735
01:18:32,080 --> 01:18:34,750
Ready to fire on your command.

736
01:18:38,550 --> 01:18:41,170
It's a match! It's a perfect match!

737
01:18:41,380 --> 01:18:43,180
- Target scanners ready, sir. 
- Fire.

738
01:19:18,130 --> 01:19:19,300
What was that?

739
01:19:19,550 --> 01:19:22,010
It's the Zeus. They're firing on the crater.

740
01:19:22,260 --> 01:19:25,680
- Aki, Captain, are you all right? 
- A little shaken. Stand by.

741
01:19:25,930 --> 01:19:30,430
Sid, the eighth spirit is not 
on our scanner. Do you have it?

742
01:19:31,020 --> 01:19:32,680
The eighth spirit...

743
01:19:33,640 --> 01:19:35,140
...has been destroyed.

744
01:19:35,810 --> 01:19:39,650
- What are we going to do now? 
- Nothing. This mission is over.

745
01:19:39,980 --> 01:19:41,780
- We have to get out of here. 
- Incoming!

746
01:20:13,640 --> 01:20:15,350
What is that?

747
01:20:15,560 --> 01:20:18,900
If you're getting us out of here, 
you better do it now.

748
01:20:30,780 --> 01:20:31,870
Hold on!

749
01:20:41,210 --> 01:20:43,170
I can't hold on to you.

750
01:20:47,800 --> 01:20:50,300
Unable to maintain altitude.

751
01:20:57,430 --> 01:20:59,940
Initiate emergency landing procedures.

752
01:21:23,750 --> 01:21:26,210
Come in. Come in, please.

753
01:21:26,460 --> 01:21:29,300
Aki, Gray, can you hear me?

754
01:21:29,550 --> 01:21:33,470
Sid, I need to talk to the station. 
Can you patch us through?

755
01:21:35,970 --> 01:21:38,890
- What is that thing? 
- I don't know, sir.

756
01:21:39,140 --> 01:21:41,350
Incoming message, sir.

757
01:21:41,600 --> 01:21:44,060
General Hein, 
You must cease fire immediately.

758
01:21:44,360 --> 01:21:48,650
What you are looking at in the crater is the 
living spirit of an alien's home world.

759
01:21:48,860 --> 01:21:51,450
Their planet was destroyed 
and part of it landed here.

760
01:21:51,700 --> 01:21:54,280
This is not an invasion. It never was.

761
01:21:54,580 --> 01:21:58,910
I see and what have we been fighting 
all this time, doctor? Ghosts?

762
01:21:59,160 --> 01:22:03,750
Yes. Spirits that are confused, 
lost and angry.

763
01:22:04,000 --> 01:22:06,670
Right. And these spirits are 
coming out of this Gaia thing.

764
01:22:06,920 --> 01:22:08,510
General Hein, you have to listen.

765
01:22:08,800 --> 01:22:12,300
Alien Gaia, Earth Gaia. 
Doctor, even if I believed in such nonsense...

766
01:22:12,640 --> 01:22:15,390
...the fact remains the Earth 
is under attack from an aggressor...

767
01:22:15,600 --> 01:22:17,890
...who must be destroyed at all costs.

768
01:22:18,180 --> 01:22:20,640
The cost may be the entire planet, sir.

769
01:22:20,980 --> 01:22:23,730
Firing on the alien Gaia will only make it stronger.

770
01:22:24,020 --> 01:22:28,320
Well, since you're under the alien's influence, doctor, 
I will take your protest to mean that we are...

771
01:22:28,570 --> 01:22:30,490
...in fact pursuing the correct course of actions.

772
01:22:30,690 --> 01:22:35,200
So i suggest you take your last few moments 
and prepare to meet your Gaia.

773
01:22:35,320 --> 01:22:38,450
Continue to fire until the invader has been destroyed.

774
01:23:15,030 --> 01:23:17,160
General, the system is overheating, sir.

775
01:23:17,370 --> 01:23:21,290
We're going to hit it again and again 
and keep on hitting it until it's dead.

776
01:23:21,580 --> 01:23:24,120
But, sir. We're not even sure 
if it's having any effect on the creature.

777
01:23:24,330 --> 01:23:27,710
No effect? We've got them on the run, soldier.

778
01:23:27,920 --> 01:23:32,010
This is our moment of victory. I order you to fire.

779
01:23:32,130 --> 01:23:35,970
- The system won't allow us to fire again. 
- We'll see about that.

780
01:23:37,180 --> 01:23:41,020
Our shield is out. We're sitting ducks in here. 
Come on!

781
01:24:02,120 --> 01:24:05,250
This is not a good place to be.

782
01:24:13,630 --> 01:24:16,630
What the hell is that? 
That's not what I think it is, Is it?

783
01:24:16,880 --> 01:24:18,090
Yes, it's Gaia.

784
01:24:18,300 --> 01:24:20,890
This is definitely not a good place to be.

785
01:24:23,060 --> 01:24:24,180
Hey, are you all right?

786
01:24:24,390 --> 01:24:28,060
I'm fine. I have to talk to Dr. Sid.

787
01:25:06,890 --> 01:25:09,440
Sid, do you read me?

788
01:25:10,100 --> 01:25:12,230
Go ahead, I'm still here.

789
01:25:12,520 --> 01:25:16,860
We're looking at Gaia. 
Do you hear me, Sid? Gaia.

790
01:25:17,070 --> 01:25:21,160
I think this explains why 
the eighth spirit appeared here.

791
01:25:22,320 --> 01:25:23,410
Yes.

792
01:25:23,950 --> 01:25:25,700
Yes, that's it!

793
01:25:25,910 --> 01:25:28,790
A Phantom must have changed into the eighth spirit...

794
01:25:28,080 --> 01:25:31,670
...when it touched a new life born from our own Gaia.

795
01:25:31,960 --> 01:25:35,210
If so, it would've been given 
a different energy signature...

796
01:25:35,420 --> 01:25:38,420
...that set it apart from the other Phantoms.

797
01:25:38,840 --> 01:25:41,890
You two could not have hoped 
for a better location...

798
01:25:42,220 --> 01:25:44,260
...to find a new compatible spirit.

799
01:25:44,470 --> 01:25:48,850
Whatever you do, don't move. 
Stay right where you are.

800
01:25:49,890 --> 01:25:53,730
Staying right where we are 
may not be as easy as it sounds.

801
01:25:53,980 --> 01:25:56,150
Don't shoot any of them!

802
01:25:56,360 --> 01:25:59,150
You could very well destroy our last hope.

803
01:25:59,320 --> 01:26:02,410
And what do you suggest I do, doctor? 
Ask them to play nice?

804
01:26:02,610 --> 01:26:06,740
Combat strategy is your area 
of expertise, captain, not mine.

805
01:26:07,120 --> 01:26:10,500
I have a reading here in the fissure. 
Do you see it?

806
01:26:10,750 --> 01:26:15,630
Yes! A compatible spirit. 
It must be very near you.

807
01:26:15,790 --> 01:26:19,130
Well? Which one is it? Which one?

808
01:26:19,340 --> 01:26:23,140
I'm having difficulty narrowing it down. 
Just a moment, please.

809
01:26:25,550 --> 01:26:29,350
Doctor, it's getting crowded in here. 
Aki, we don't have much time. Aki.

810
01:28:01,190 --> 01:28:03,440
With the hope of new life...

811
01:28:03,650 --> 01:28:06,700
...has Gaia changed 
the Phantom within?

812
01:28:12,830 --> 01:28:14,120
I have it.

813
01:28:20,340 --> 01:28:23,130
Gray, get in here. I need you!

814
01:28:23,920 --> 01:28:26,970
Do you hear me, Sid? 
The wave pattern is complete.

815
01:28:27,180 --> 01:28:30,430
Yes, I read you. This is wonderful.

816
01:28:30,640 --> 01:28:33,520
I don't see how you could have found the final spirit.

817
01:28:33,770 --> 01:28:36,140
It found me, doctor.

818
01:28:38,020 --> 01:28:39,650
Oh, my word.

819
01:28:40,900 --> 01:28:43,980
I see now. I understand.

820
01:28:44,190 --> 01:28:46,820
Well, I don't understand! 
What the hell is going on?

821
01:28:47,030 --> 01:28:49,030
Give me the ovo-pac. 
I need to project the completed wave.

822
01:28:49,240 --> 01:28:52,490
- But we'll be defenseless. 
- Just do it!

823
01:28:52,700 --> 01:28:54,580
I hope you know 
what you're doing, Aki.

824
01:28:54,580 --> 01:28:57,080
- We can use the shield to project the wave. 
- What?

825
01:28:57,290 --> 01:29:00,790
Dr. Sid's theory was right. 
I have it. The eighth spirit.

826
01:29:01,000 --> 01:29:02,380
I'm cured, Gray.

827
01:29:02,540 --> 01:29:05,630
- Are you sure you have the final spirit? 
- Yes, I'm sure.

828
01:29:06,010 --> 01:29:09,130
- But how? How can you know that? 
- Don't worry. A Phantom told me.

829
01:29:09,340 --> 01:29:10,970
Oh, great.

830
01:29:11,350 --> 01:29:13,470
That's it. Shield on.

831
01:29:19,350 --> 01:29:22,270
It's not working. 
We have to do something before it's too late.

832
01:29:22,520 --> 01:29:25,610
If this doesn't work, 
then it's already too late.

833
01:29:33,580 --> 01:29:35,040
Gray, trust me.

834
01:29:59,940 --> 01:30:01,730
I'll blast you all to hell.

835
01:30:09,400 --> 01:30:11,030
Oh, no. No!

836
01:30:15,410 --> 01:30:16,660
Get down!

837
01:30:29,170 --> 01:30:32,180
- Warning. System overload. 
- I know.

838
01:30:32,380 --> 01:30:35,260
- Warning. System overload. 
- I know!

839
01:30:40,680 --> 01:30:42,690
But it must be done.

840
01:31:25,400 --> 01:31:26,440
Fire.

841
01:31:26,650 --> 01:31:28,360
Fire, damn you!

842
01:31:29,400 --> 01:31:30,530
Fire!

843
01:32:48,730 --> 01:32:50,940
Don't leave me, Gray.

844
01:32:52,150 --> 01:32:54,780
Told Sid this was a one-way trip.

845
01:32:55,610 --> 01:32:57,200
Looks like I was right.

846
01:32:57,570 --> 01:32:59,950
No, Gray. Hang on, please.

847
01:33:00,160 --> 01:33:02,080
I still have the wave.

848
01:33:02,280 --> 01:33:04,330
We can get through this.

849
01:33:09,170 --> 01:33:11,460
- We're not gonna make it. 
- We're going to make it.

850
01:33:11,710 --> 01:33:13,840
We both know that isn't true.

851
01:33:27,310 --> 01:33:28,560
Help me.

852
01:33:38,990 --> 01:33:40,780
Listen to me.

853
01:33:40,990 --> 01:33:45,120
You saved my life once. 
Now I want you to save yourself.

854
01:33:45,370 --> 01:33:47,080
Gray, no. Please?

855
01:33:47,330 --> 01:33:50,580
Let me do this, Aki. Trust me.

856
01:34:00,550 --> 01:34:02,180
Don't leave me, Gray.

857
01:34:02,470 --> 01:34:05,310
You've been trying to tell me that death isn't the end.

858
01:34:05,600 --> 01:34:10,480
Don't back out on me now that I finally believe.

859
01:34:22,320 --> 01:34:23,450
I love you.

860
01:36:12,970 --> 01:36:14,930
Oh, it's warm.
